  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-least-priv",
      "text": "**Least-privilege auditor**: mechanical scans for privilege anti-patterns,\nplus the four-question permission gate. Sovereignty is built in — all power\nbelongs to the operator; autonomy lives only inside the granted scope; any\nprivilege escalation requires a fresh explicit grant, never self-service."
    },
    {
      "section": "Anti-patterns scanned",
      "text": "| Family | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| hardened-escalation | `sudo` · `chmod 777` · plaintext credentials |\n| root-traces | hardcoded `/root/...` · granting sudo to users |\n| wide-writes | `rm -rf /` (red-line class) |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Four-question gate",
      "text": "1. Does this piece truly need the privilege?\n2. Can the privilege be narrowed?\n3. What happens on overreach?\n4. When is it revoked?"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install & use",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin add github:<owner>/dsh-least-priv\ncurl \"http://127.0.0.1:<port>/least-priv/api?act=four\"\ncurl \"http://127.0.0.1:<port>/least-priv/api?act=scan&path=/path/to/code\"\n```"
    }
  ],
